A template `if` includes its body only when a `Bool` condition is true.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    [if signed_in:
        Welcome back
    ]
]

An option-present capture includes its body only when the option has a value.
The captured value is available inside that body.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    [if maybe_name is |name|:
        Hello [name]
    ]
]

Template `if` has no `else` or `else if` form. Template loops repeat content
with an ordinary loop header.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    [loop names |name|:
        <p>Hello [name]</p>
    ]
]

Template control flow has no `break` or `continue` markers. Ordinary Moth
statements still have their own `if`, `else`, `break` and `continue` forms.
Template bodies build lazily at runtime unless they are const-required.
